TEXT -448 -224 Left 2 ;Common base / gate: the base/gate is grounded for the signal (CB/CG) and the input goes into the emitter/source through CIN, from a 50 Ω source (RSIG). The bias is the same as in the common emitter.\nRin ≈ 1/gm: ≈ 18 Ω (BJT) or ≈ 120 Ω (MOSFET), so it needs a low-impedance source. Av = (RC ∥ RL) / (RSIG + 1/gm): ≈ 45 (33 dB) for the BJT and ≈ 17 (25 dB) for the MOSFET, without inversion.\nThere is no Miller effect (no capacitance from the output back to the input), which is why it is used at high frequency and, on top of a common emitter, in the cascode.
TEXT -320 -64 Left 2 ;BJT: BC547C
TEXT 640 -64 Left 2 ;MOSFET: 2N7000
